      "side": 1,
      "message": "Previously refresh() guaranteed a new job started after the workspace refresh, so joining it meant \"diff reflects the refreshed state\". Now:\n\n-  if a reload is already RUNNING, join() waits for a computation that started before the resource refresh, and the (correct) re-run happens asynchronously afterwards;\n-  if the running job just finished, reloadJob may be null and the join is skipped entirely.\n\nSince rerunIfRequested() schedules the follow-up job before the first job leaves RUNNING, a family join is race-free and restores the old guarantee:\n\n\nSo instead of \n\nJob next \u003d reloadJob;\nif (next !\u003d null) next.join();\n\nthis below should be used now:\nJob.getJobManager().join(JobFamilies.INDEX_DIFF_CACHE_UPDATE, monitor);",
      "revId": "85fa0d63537875aaa8f9a2d8ca956135911aa15a",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
